e(String)I`, D25 Clojure `parse_frame` (unguarded `RT.nth(v,4)` vs `(< 4 (count v))` guard -> -1); reachability = the env compares in `-main`; native twins: `objdump -d` per symbol + `diff`, `rz-diff -t functions a b` |\n146\t| V language ELF (D27: `main__main`, `_vinit`/`_vcleanup`, `builtin__*`/`strconv__*`/`Array_string_*`, `_const_<mod>__<name>` data symbols, `V panic: `, bundled Boehm `GC_*` + `GC_TRACE`, `builtin__print_backtrace*`) | C-backend language: plain ELF (`elf`/62) for header ids; HCFG RAW appended at image_end (`grep -abo HCFG F` = EOF-379); a gcc `-flto -Os` build keeps ~200 syms (main__main inlined away), the tcc build ~1900 |\n147\t| Odin ELF (D28: strings `/odin/base/runtime/*.odin`, `base/runtime: getrandom failed`; glibc PIE, NEEDED libm/libc/ld-linux-x86-64, STRIPPED (~20 `.dynsym` entries, no `.symtab`), ~22 KB) | Plain ELF (`elf`/62) for header ids; HCFG RAW appended exactly at image_end (`e_shoff+e_shnum*64`, `grep -abo HCFG F`), same \"scan backward from the end\" rule as D27 |\n148\t| N look-alike members (`-family-a`/`-family-b`/`-false-friend`, same size + section table) or \"cluster by behavior\", \"false friends\", \"family vs strangers\" | Per pair `cmp -l A B \\| wc -l` (D28: a vs b = 1 byte, the role string `huntress-role-<role>`; false friend ~2k bytes from `.text` on), sha256 of `.text`/`.rodata` per member, HCFG per member (the false friend has its OWN valid config, campaign `FF28-` vs `BR28-`), trace records (`branch`/`event_count`). Route ids by role; family consensus = the NAMED members only |\n149\t| Backfill question \"Evaluate this public predicate ...\", \"count names that match /re/\", \"sort ..., join with one LF ..., SHA-256\", \"join those digests with ASCII colon\" | The sentence is the spec: `lib.binary.generic_field(blob, suffix, question, member)`; ELF symbol names = `.symtab` (`.dynsym` only if no `.symtab`); \"final bytes contain\" = Latin-1 (+ UTF-16LE when stated) substring |\n150\t| Same-source builds named by their COMPILER (`-gcc.elf`/`-tcc.elf`; next clang / zig cc / msvc / mingw) or \"name the toolchain\", \"runtime and linker fingerprints\" | Header + consensus HCFG per member as usual (D27 asked nothing else). Attribution facts if asked: `readelf --debug-dump=info F \\| grep -m2 producer` (gcc: `GNU C99 12.2.1 20220924 ... -Os -std=c99`, `GNU AS 2.40`); `.comment` was ABSENT on both; gcc = DWARF 5 (`.debug_line_str`/`.debug_loclists`), IPA suffixes `.lto_priv.N`/`.constprop.N`/`.isra.N`, FILE `crtstuff.c`, `.eh_frame_hdr`+`.gnu.hash`; tcc = STABS (`.stab`/`.stabstr`, no DWARF), `.hash` only, unmerged input sections (`.text._start_c`, `.rodata.str1.1`, `.data.ro`, `.data.rel.ro.local`), one NT_GNU_PROPERTY note per input object (4), `tcc_backtrace`/`tcc_state`, 4x the size; libc = PT_INTERP `/lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1` + NEEDED `libc.musl-x86_64.so.1`, musl src path `/home/buildozer/aports/main/musl/src/1.2.4` (Alpine) |\n151\t| Swift ELF (`swift5_*` sections, `$s<len><Module>` symbols, 60+ MB) | Never eager-parse symbols; regex `SENGR` base64 in `.rodata`; `bin/swift-demangle` |\n152\t| Nim / D / Crystal / Free Pascal / ObjC / Ada / Fortran ELF (`NimMain`; `_D4core`; `Crystal:H`; `FPC 3.2.2`; `__objc_*`; `GNAT Version`; `libgfortran.so.5`) | Plain ELF (`elf`/`x86-64`/`62`), carried-over solver; HCFG base64 `SENGR...` (Nim/D/Crystal, offset = the `S`; Nim has raw decoys) or RAW (FPC `.data`, ObjC `.hcfg`, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`; offset = the `H`) |\n153\t| GnuCOBOL (`libcob.so.1`, `cob_init`) / Haskell GHC (`Main_main*_closure`, z-encoded `ghczminternal_*`, `GHC 9.x`) / OCaml (`caml_startup`, `camlStdlib__*`, `4.02.3`; `.cmxs` = natdynlink ET_DYN plugin, dynsyms `caml_plugin_header`, magic `Caml2007D002`) | Plain ELF for header ids; config NOT in the image for COBOL/Haskell (PK19/RS20 overlay past the section-header table, D19/D20); OCaml: HCFG RAW in the plugin `.data`; `nm -D --defined-only`, `readelf -dW` for exports/NEEDED |\n154\t| File size > `e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize` (or > max section end), with or without a crc-valid HCFG | Appended OVERLAY: `xxd -s <image_end> F`; magic `<2 caps><day>` (`PK19` D19, `RS20` D20); parse the header fields the question lists, verify its bounds/sha256, run its transform if any, HCFG at the stated offset. A raw HCFG hit INSIDE the overlay (D20) still needs the header fields (`hcfg_resource_size`, offsets) |\n155\t| `00 61 73 6d 01 00 00 00` (`\\0asm`), `.wasm` | `lib.binary.wasm_layout(data)` or `wasm-objdump -x f.wasm`; format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32`; HCFG RAW in data segment 0 |\n156\t| `NEKO` magic / `.n` file (format enum lists `neko_bytecode` since D19) | Neko VM bytecode (Haxe/nekoc): `neko`/`haxe` are apt-installable; globals table holds the string constants -> HCFG scan; format `neko_bytecode` |\n157\t| `kind: enum` + `accepted_values` + \"Apply these mutually exclusive rules in order\", or text describing bytes (\"Read k1 at +5 ... ror8(byte XOR k2,3) XOR k1 ... verify the SHA-256\") | The question IS the spec (D17, D19): implement it literally over the parsed facts, emit one listed token; don't reverse the stub first |\n158\t| Packed / high entropy / `UPX!`; or a real code-reversing question | `lib.binary.packer_info` -> `upx -d` on a COPY (UPX unseen); `rizin -q -c \"aaa; pdf @ sym.<fn>\"`; Ghidra headless `lib.binary.ghidra_decompile` (last resort) |\n159\t\n160\t## Day by day\n161\t**D1 \"ELF Aware\"** (~14 min, 4 wrong): C ELF64 headers, `.huntress`, recover_code. **D2 \"Mangled\"** (~22 min): C++ ELF/MinGW PE,\n162\tfirst HCFG; PE symbols = COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`. **D3 \"Table Manners\"** (~1 h 48 min, ~60 wrong): .NET, format `pe_cli` after ~50\n163\tsynonyms. **D4 \"Go Fish\"** (1.5 min): `amd64` REJECTED → `x86-64`. **D5 \"Rust Belt\"** (7 s). **D6 \"Pool Party\"** (~5 min): jar\n164\tconstant-pool base64 HCFG. **D7 \"Routine Check\"** (3 min): Kotlin fat jar. **D8 \"Swift Justice\"**: 67 MB Swift; backfill #1 to 10\n165\tids/group; integer elf_class/machine. **D9 \"Nimble\"** (86 s): raw decoys, NEW `hcfg_offset`. **D10 \"Zig Zag\"** (33 s): NEW\n166\t`has_hcfg_section`. **D11 \"D-Day\"** (36 s). **D12 \"Pascal's Wager\"** (54 s): HCFG RAW. **D13 \"Crystal Clear\"** (14 s). **D14\n167\t\"Selective Memory\"** (9 s): ObjC, `.hcfg`. **D15 \"Stripped\"** (74 s): stripped/symbolized pair, `<qualifier>_` ids. **D16 \"Wasm\n168\tUp\"** (91 s): compact/direct wasm pair, `wasm`/`wasm32` first try via the prebuilt `wasm_layout`.\n169\t**D17 \"Decoder Ring\"** (204 Qs): Ada; backfill #2; `hcfg_storage` burned ~10.9k POSTs / 3.5 h until revised to an enum.\n170\t**D18 \"Flow State\"** (T+11 s): Fortran, call-graph theme unasked. **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"** (T+2:25): GnuCOBOL + `PK19` packed\n171\toverlay; NEW `overlay_offset`/`overlay_size`; the questions spelled the stub. **D20 \"Resourceful\"** (T+49 s): Haskell + `RS20`\n172\toverlay; NEW `hcfg_resource_size`. **D21 \"Shared Custody\"** (T+1:33): OCaml loader + `.cmxs` plugin; question-named member\n173\trouting AFTER the qualifier peel (running it first dropped 26 ids).\n174\t\n175\t**D22 \"Bridge Troll\"** (T+47 s): F# dll + runtimeconfig + `FSharp.Core.dll` support member; HCFG RAW twice (\"FIRST record\n176\tthat validates\"); basenames `variant-000` -> `sample`. **D23 \"Trust Issues\"** (T+84 s): VB.NET, HCFG as PE overlay; timed modes\n177\tre-shaped values. **D24 \"Spot the Difference\"** (T+35 s): Scala twin jars `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`, the 12-id twin template\n178\t(role `<role>_format`, consensus config_*). **D25 \"Out of Bounds\"** (T+80 s): Clojure twins; Mastery 9 sets first POST\n179\tcross-wired 55 ids (`id(bytes)` caches) -> CORRECT ~2 min via localize + live worker.\n180\t\n181\t**D26 \"Crash Course\"** (312 Qs; T+76 s, 0 wrong): Groovy 4 jar + `crash/trace.json` sidecar; theme ASKED (`crash_fault_method` =\n182\tframes[0], `crash_frames_match_methods`); ~15 lines for the sidecar. Insight: read the question before reversing. **D27 \"Compiler\n183\tSays What\"** (324 Qs; T+56 s, 0 wrong, ZERO new code): V-language gcc/tcc twin ELFs, HCFG RAW appended at image_end, \"scan\n184\tbackward from the end\"; attribution theme UNASKED (facts in Recognition cues).\n185\t\n186\t**D28 \"Family Resemblance\"** (slug `family-clustering`; 392 Qs; **CORRECT T+3:23, 6 rejected POSTs (4 batches + 2 single-id)**; TT 54 s / Mastery\n187\t12 sets (4704 ids) CORRECT first POST).\n188\t- Artifact: an Odin ELF TRIO in archive order `d28--sample-false-friend.elf`, `-family-a.elf`, `-family-b.elf` (~22.9 KB each,\n189\t  glibc PIE, stripped, identical section table). a vs b differ in ONE byte (role string); the false friend differs in ~2k bytes\n190\t  from `.text` on and carries its own valid HCFG (campaign `FF28-`). HCFG RAW appended at e_shoff+e_shnum*64 in all three.\n191\t- 14 new ids: 3 sha256, `<role>_format`/`<role>_machine` for `false_friend`/`family_a`/`family_b` (integer 62), 4 unqualified\n192\t  config_* = consensus of family-a + family-b (\"do not use false-friend.elf\"), `false_friend_config_campaign`. The cluster/\n193\t  similarity theme itself was NOT asked beyond that routing.\n194\t- BACKFILL #3 was the real work: 54 new spec-worded ids padded d01-d27 to 14 each (see Variant axes). The D27 solver answered\n195\t  361/392; the race harness banked 324 carried-over ids at T+1:06 and 36 more by T+1:23 (bisected batches); a worker added\n196\t  the 31 missing fields (generic spec-grammar fallback) and POSTed at T+2:34; last id at T+3:23.\n197\t- Lost time: four all-or-nothing batches sank on ONE wrong backfill field each -- d20 `overlay_size` (generic `<2 caps><2\n198\t  digits>` match -> 19; right = len - rfind(`RS20`) = 463) and d13 `crystal_symbol_count` (1255 with `.dynsym` added; right =\n199\t  771 from `.symtab` only, re-derived in 44 s). TT: d10 re-rolled to a PE `.exe` and the ELF-worded\n200\t  `section_count` was empty -> a live worker answered NumberOfSections (9). Mastery: the post-run replay of 10-12-set\n201\t  cases hit the 8 s timeout under load (pyelftools `.symtab` parse ~1 s/set) -> struct-parsed symtab reader, ~1 s/set total.\n202\t\n203\t## GM answer conventions learned\n204\t| Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |\n205\t|---|---|---|\n206\t| elf_class | exact_text: `ELF64`/`ELF32` (readelf style); `kind: integer` (D8+): the bit width `64`/`32` | ELFCLASS64; `2`/`1` |\n207\t| machine (`kind: integer`, D8-D9, D15, D21 loader/plugin, D27 gcc/tcc) | decimal e_machine (`62` = x86-64), also for an ET_DYN `.cmxs`; same for every compiler of one source | — |\n208\t| endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |\n209\t| machine (ELF) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` (D19 text: tool labels and decimal/hex codes also accepted) | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 (pre-D17 exact_text) |\n210\t| machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c → `i386`; 0x8664 → `x86-64` | x86 (for PE i386); raw `0x8664` |\n211\t| architecture | the same machine words (Go amd64 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\n212\t| elf_type | `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |\n213\t| entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |\n214\t| recover_code (`kind: integer`) | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the symbol is absent (stripped d01) | the stripped/renamed leaf's constant (8114, 8106) |\n215\t| has_symtab / has_cpp_* / has_go_runtime / has_rust_mangled_symbol / has_coroutine_runtime | enum `true`/`false` | — |\n216\t| marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if the section is missing | — |\n217\t| format (enum since D17-D19 on d12+) | `elf`, `pe`, `pe_cli` (.NET), `jar`, `wasm`, `neko_bytecode` (listed, unseen) | ELF, ELF64, elf64-x86-64, exe, pe32+, jar_jvm, ~50 .NET synonyms |\n218\t| format / arch per container (language/compiler never changes the label) | compiled ELF (D8-D21, D27 V via gcc AND tcc) `elf`/`x86-64`; WASM `wasm`/`wasm32`; .NET any language (C#, F#, VB.NET) `pe_cli`/`i386`; any JVM jar (Java, Kotlin, Scala D24, Clojure D25, Groovy D26, `<role>_format` too) `jar` | x86 for PE i386 |\n219\t| C++ symbols (ELF) incl. `mangled_score_symbol`, `typeinfo_symbol` (D17) | bare Itanium mangled name (`_ZNK15DiscoveryEngine5scoreEPKc`, `_ZTI15DiscoveryEngine`) | the demangled form |\n220\t| C++ symbols (PE/MinGW) | COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>` / `.rdata$<mangled>` | bare mangled name |\n221\t| section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\"\"` (D17 text: omitting it also accepted) | list without \"\" (pre-D17) |\n222\t| symbols (JSON) | non-empty .symtab names, table order, dupes kept | list with the \"\" entries |\n223\t| disassembly (JSON) | capstone intel `\"mov eax, 8100\"`, `\"ret\"`, decimal immediates | hex imm, `\"ret \"` |\n224\t| methods / access_flags / method_count (jar, D17; d26 D26) | Main-Class `method_info` names in table order incl. `<init>` (JSON) / decimal `49` / count incl. `<init>`/`<clinit>` and compiler synthetics (Groovy `$getStaticMetaClass`, `$getLookup`, getters: d26 = 10) | — |\n225\t| crash_fault_method / crash_frames_match_methods (D26) | trace.json `frames[0]` verbatim (bare method name `stageThree`) / `true`/`false` = every frame in the primary class's method-name set | — |\n226\t| metadata_version (d03, d22 F#, d23 VB.NET) | BSJB root string `v4.0.30319` (same for every .NET language) | net8.0 / TFM |\n227\t| config_* | values verbatim from the decoded HCFG JSON (mutex keeps ONE backslash); D19: from the UNPACKED overlay's HCFG; D21: from the member the question names (plugin); D24/D25/D27 unqualified = consensus of both twins | JSON-escaped `\\\\`; `none` when the blob is merely hidden (D19) |\n228\t| hcfg_version / xor_key_hex | header byte 4 decimal / header byte 5 as `0x%02x` | — |\n229\t| has_hcfg_section (enum) | `true` when a section is literally named `.hcfg` | — |\n230\t| hcfg_offset (integer) | decimal FILE offset: base64 text start (`S`), RAW = the `HCFG` magic | — |\n231\t| overlay_offset / overlay_size (integer, D19-D20) | offset of the LAST occurrence of the day's overlay magic (`PK19`, `RS20`) / file length - that offset (header included) | — |\n232\t| hcfg_resource_size (integer, D20) | the overlay header's u32le resource-length field (RS20+8) in base 10 = the HCFG record length (12 + payload) | overlay size, payload-only length (not tried, but distinct values) |\n233\t| hcfg_storage (enum, D17) | `base64`, `raw_hcfg_section`, `raw_const_array`, `wasm_data_segment`, `raw` | every free-text spelling (~10.9k probes) -- closed token set |\n234\t| compression_methods (jar, json) | sorted distinct ZIP method ids, compact: `[0,8]` (names also accepted) | — |\n235\t| D28 backfill #3 counts (integer) | `symbol_count`/`d_symbol_count`/`crystal_symbol_count`/`handler_symbol_count` over NONEMPTY `.symtab` names (dupes kept; `.dynsym` only when no `.symtab`); `section_count` = ELF e_shnum incl. index 0 (PE re-roll: FILE_HEADER.NumberOfSections); `class_count` = `.class` entries in the jar CD; `structural_artifact_count` = group members | d13 count with `.dynsym` added (1255) |\n236\t| D28 hashes / predicates | `handler_symbols_sha256` = sha256(LF-join(sorted matches)), `method_names_sha256` over UNIQUE names; `structural_ordered_set_sha256` = sha256(\":\".join(member sha256 hex in CD order)); `has_*_runtime`/`has_decoy_branch` = literal substring predicate as stated -> `true`/`false` | — |\n237\t| D28 header / identity text | `cli_runtime` = CLI header `Major.Minor` (`2.5` for every .NET group); `vtable_symbol` = first symtab name matching the regex, bare on ELF (`_ZTV15DiscoveryEngine`), section-prefixed on PE; `class_name` = Main-Class `this_class` internal name (`Day06Variant000`); `packing_key_1/2_hex` = PK19 k1/k2 `0x%02x`; `plugin_hcfg_offset` = the `H` | d20 `overlay_size` from a non-day magic (19) |\n238\t| machine / format wording (D28 reworded) | machine (pattern): label, readelf/objdump/file label, or decimal/hex code all accepted; d10 format: ELF/PE in any case or ELF64/PE32+/\"Portable Executable\"; `<role>_machine` integer stays decimal (`62`) | — |\n239\tNaming law (from playbook.py): native format = container only; a managed .NET binary = container_runtime (pe+cli).\n240\tJava broke the compound law (`jar`); bytecode VMs get `<vm>_bytecode` (`neko_bytecode` in the D19 enum).\n241\t\n242\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n243\t- **A synthetic label with no derivable spelling** (D3 .NET format ~1.5 h; D17 raw `hcfg_storage`, ~10.9k POSTs over 3.5 h,\n244\t  solved only by the organizers' contract revision): stop after ~10 single-id probes plus one `hctf labels` run, write HELP.md,\n245\t  then RE-PULL THE CONTRACT periodically and diff each id's question/answer_format. Never mass-probe an exact_text label.\n246\t- **Reversing what the question already specifies** (D19): the questions gave offsets, transform and hash check; guessing from\n247\t  bytes produced a spurious partial HCFG. Read the longest question of each new family FIRST. Size fields = the exact header\n248\t  field the layout names (D20 `hcfg_resource_size` = u32 @+8, not overlay/JSON length).\n249\t- **Absence vs hidden**: `none`/`[]`/`false` is right when the thing is ABSENT (stripped d01, a re-asked field inherits it),\n250\t  wrong when it is merely HIDDEN (D19 config: packed; the race harness's `none` placeholders were rejected).\n251\t- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the set and hides which one (D2; D28: 4 batches sank on 2\n252\t  generic-heuristic backfill fields, T+3:23 instead of ~T+1:30). POST carried-over ids first (they bank as `accepted`), then\n253\t  each NEW field family ALONE or bisect on the first rejection; a heuristic answer to a new spec is a guess until accepted.\n254\t- **Support members** (D3, D22): answer only from the PRIMARY assembly/classfile, but hash every member in archive order; skip\n255\t  a 5.7 MB framework DLL in brute passes.\n256\t- **\"The theme is never asked\" is NOT a rule** (D26): after 5 unasked days the crash theme was asked via a JSON sidecar inside\n257\t  the jar; the carried-over solver had no field for it (+31 s for a worker). On every new day list the member's NON-code entries\n258\t  (`unzip -l`, sections, resources, overlays) and parse any JSON/text sidecar up front. Unasked again on D27 (attribution).\n259\t- **Theme facts / must-not-run samples**: record each day's theme facts (D21 NEEDED/exports ... D26 trace + thrower, D27 producer/\n260\t  linker/libc per build) in NOTES.md; PROVE statically, never run the jar/ELF; a verdict id = evaluate the predicate table.\n261\t- **Per-member caches keyed on `id(bytes)`** (D25 Mastery, 55 wrong ids in 5/9 sets): CPython reuses a freed object's address,\n262\t  so a later member inherits an earlier member's facts. Symptom: wrong values that are VALID answers for another `dNN--` group\n263\t  of the same delivery. Key on (delivery, member name) / sha256 or pin the bytes (fixed; D26 10 sets clean).\n264\t- **Formatting / routing**: build submit JSON with python/jq (mutex = ONE backslash); capstone `ret` without trailing space,\n265\t  decimal imms; peel the (longest, multi-word) member qualifier before declaring a field unknown (D15, D28 `family_a`), the\n266\t  question-named-member router runs AFTER that peel (D21 dropped 26 ids), read `answer_format.kind` per id (D8).\n267\t- **Archives**: never unzip recursively (nested .jar/.apk lose their `dNN--` prefix); jar members are deflated, so `grep HCFG\n268\t  file.jar` finds nothing -- inflate every class (Scala `$` module, Clojure `__init`, Groovy static field) and non-class entry.\n269\t  Huge members (D8 67 MB Swift): no per-key brute force or per-field re-parse; cheap encodings first, crc-gate every hit.\n270\t- **Decoy magics** (D9 Nim): code that CHECKS the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` literals; len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes! Require non-empty\n271\t  JSON that parses, keep scanning. Scan DIRECTION is part of the spec (D22 \"first ... that validates\" from the start, D27 \"scan\n272\t  backward from the end\"): with two valid records they pick different ones -- follow the question per id. Overlays: \"final\" -> `rfind`, verify the stated sha256. Offsets from `re.finditer().start()`\n273\t  on BOTH raw and base64 paths (D12), not `strings -t d` (off by 1).\n274\t- **ELF-worded id on a PE re-roll** (D28 TT d10 `.exe`): the solver left `section_count` empty -> live worker (+~40 s). Every\n275\t  ELF header/section/symbol field needs a PE mapping (NumberOfSections, COFF symbols, OptionalHeader) because members re-roll.\n276\t- **Timed windows**: download dominates (D16 TT 52 s of 64 s; D25 single ~69 s of 80 s). WASM sizes = 5-byte PADDED LEB128;\n277\t  PE machine map must include 0x8664 -> `x86-64` (a replay emitted `0x8664` and failed TT twice).\n278\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"964dc59f-c591-45ab-b64c-46b6ec05cc87","uuid":"49d97754-595b-4beb-b652-5ac36f27d48c","timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:04:35.739Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/964dc59f-c591-45ab-b64c-46b6ec05cc87/tool-results/b14yf9yj5.txt","content":"# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-28; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure, degrade per field.\n- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`), CUMULATIVE from D3: one group per past day (`dNN--sample.<ext>`, `variant-000`\n  before D22) + ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF/MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET, D4 Go, D5 Rust, D6 Java jar,\n  D7 Kotlin jar, D8 Swift (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig, D11 D, D12 FPC, D13 Crystal, D14 ObjC, D15 C `-stripped`/`-symbolized`, D16\n  WASM `-compact`/`-direct`, D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + `PK19` overlay, D20 Haskell + `RS20` overlay, D21 OCaml\n  `-loader.elf` + `-plugin.cmxs`, D22 F# (+ `FSharp.Core.dll`), D23 VB.NET, D24 Scala jar PAIR `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`, D25\n  Clojure jar PAIR, D26 Groovy jar (+ `crash/trace.json` entry), D27 V-language ELF PAIR `-gcc.elf`/`-tcc.elf` (one V source,\n  two C backends, both musl-dynamic x86-64), **D28 Odin ELF TRIO `-family-a.elf`/`-family-b.elf`/`-false-friend.elf` (22 KB\n  glibc PIEs, stripped, same size and layout; a/b differ in ONE byte, the false friend in ~2k bytes + its own config)**.\n  Since D18 each day = a THEME on a new language: call graph (D18), packing (D19), resources/overlays (D20), shared libraries\n  (D21), managed<->native bridge (D22), anti-analysis (D23), PATCH DIFFING (D24), BOUNDS-ERROR ROOT CAUSE + reachability (D25),\n  CRASH TRIAGE (D26), COMPILER ATTRIBUTION (D27 \"name the toolchain\"), **FAMILY CLUSTERING (D28 \"These binaries might be related\n  -- or they might just look alike. Cluster them by behavior, watch out for false friends, and sort the family from the\n  strangers\")**. D24-D26 = vuln arc (3 days); D27-D28 = ATTRIBUTION arc (toolchain -> family). 3 days left: expect the arc's\n  3rd step (variant/lineage ordering, shared-code/similarity measures, YARA-style family signature) or a capstone/backfill on\n  D31. Language track: D27 V and D28 Odin = niche native languages (both predicted by the atlas). Left: Hare, Vala/Genie, C3,\n  Cython, hxcpp, Haxe->Neko (`neko_bytecode` still in the enum, unseen), Elixir/BEAM, niche JVM.\n  Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; multi-member groups add `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` (D15/D16/D21/D24/\n  D25/D27/D28; hyphenated roles become underscores: `family-a.elf` -> `d28_analysis_family_a_machine`, `false_friend_*`) and\n  unqualified ids whose QUESTION names the member (D21) or demands consensus of the NAMED subset (D24/D25/D27 both twins; D28\n  \"Decode family-a.elf and family-b.elf ... do not use false-friend.elf\").\n- From D2 every new member embeds the **HCFG** blob `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16le len | u32le crc32(plain) | xor'd JSON\n  @12`; only its STORAGE changes (see Variant axes). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND base64 `SENGR...`, crc-gate every hit; when\n  both miss, look past the image end (overlay) and read the question. Parse the whole JSON dict (never-asked keys exist).\n- The hard part is the GM's label for `exact_text` fields; **the organizers RE-ISSUE the contract** when a label is unguessable\n  (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> enum + ordered rules). Since D24 EVERY question is a full SPEC (sha256 \"ZIP central-directory order ...\n  member K (1-based)\", format rule list, HCFG layout + carrier rule, JAR \"Base64-alphabet UTF-8 constants >= 80 characters ...\n  first CRC32-valid\", D26 \"Parse crash/trace.json ... first string in its frames array\", D27 \"Scan backward from the end\").\n- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19 \"RS20 for Day 20\", d07 \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit\" (both\n  came true). Open after D28: enum `neko_bytecode` (D22-D28 added no new token/day). Grep each contract for `[A-Z]{2}\\d\\d`, `Day NN`, unseen enum values.\n- **Theme asked on its own group only sometimes**: D19/D20 yes (overlay fields), D21-D25 NO, D26 YES (`crash_fault_method`,\n  `crash_frames_match_methods`, from a JSON SIDECAR inside the member), D27 NO (compiler fingerprints unasked), **D28 ONLY via\n  routing** (family consensus config_* + `false_friend_config_campaign`; no similarity/cluster field). 14 ids = 3 sha256 +\n  `<role>_format`/`<role>_machine` x3 + 4 family-consensus config_* + 1 false_friend config.\n- **Every member embeds a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template** (unasked) {branch, event_count, campaign, family\n  `<lang>_<theme>_trace`, effects, network none} gated on env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (+ `HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT` D25-D26); family\n  NAMES THE THEME: D25 `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`, D26 `groovy_synthetic_crash_trace` (+ `huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`\n  sidecar), D27 `v_cross_backend_attribution_trace`/`equivalent_behavior_only`, D28 `odin_family_cluster_trace`/\n  `behavior_cluster_only` + `cluster_marker_positive` (4 records per member; the false friend's event_counts differ) -- grep\n  `_trace\"` to read the day's theme.\n- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160, D17 204 (backfill #2), +12/day to D27 324, **D28 392 = 28 groups x 14 (BACKFILL #3:\n  54 new ids pad EVERY old group to 14, all spelled as specs -- public predicates, regex counts, sorted-join sha256)**. Mastery =\n  `setN.` copies, +1 set/day (**D28 12 sets = 4704 ids, ~17 MB per delivery**). Timed: D26 TT 5.3 s / M 8.2 s; D27 TT 5.4 s /\n  M 14.5 s; **D28 TT 54 s (live worker: d10 re-rolled to PE) / Mastery CORRECT first POST (solve 2.4 s, submit 4.9 s)**.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, storage per container: `.hcfg` section (D2/D10/D14), .NET FieldRVA (D3), Go/Rust\n  rodata, base64 in a jar constant pool (Java/Kotlin, D24 Scala `$` module, D25 Clojure `<ns>__init.class` `encoded-config` Var,\n  D26 Groovy `static final String encodedConfig` in the Main-Class) / Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW FPC `.data`, WASM data seg 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay, D20 RS20 overlay,\n  D21 OCaml plugin `.data`, D22 F# RAW twice (`.text` + PE overlay: \"FIRST record that validates\"), D23 VB.NET RAW PE overlay,\n  D27 V gcc+tcc RAW appended EXACTLY at `e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize` with NO day magic (the file ends with the record) and the\n  question rule reversed: \"Scan backward from the end of the member for literal HCFG magic and accept the first CRC32-valid\".\n  Rule: scan for `HCFG` and `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (jars: every class's constant pool), accept only crc32(plain) match AND\n  parsing JSON, keep scanning past failures (D9 Nim decoys); scan in the DIRECTION the question states (D22 first-from-start,\n  D27 `rfind` loop from EOF); never a fixed offset or a fixed class. Storage never changed WITHIN a day (single/TT/all Mastery sets).\n- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- appended at `e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize`, magic `<2 caps><day>`, header\n  spelled by the QUESTION: PK19 `magic|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le packed_len @8|sha256(unpacked) @12|packed @44`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`;\n  RS20 `magic|ver @4|u32le resource_len @8|u16le scratch_len @12|sha256(scratch) @16|HCFG @48 raw|scratch`. Rule: `o =\n  data.rfind(magic)` (\"final\"), parse the listed widths, verify bounds + hash; unspecified transform -> known-plaintext `HCFG`.\n- **Location / storage as answer** -- `hcfg_offset` = decimal FILE offset (base64 -> the `S`, RAW -> the `H`); `overlay_offset` =\n  the magic, `overlay_size` = len - offset; `hcfg_resource_size` = the u32le @+8 (380). `hcfg_storage` (D17 enum) in order:\n  `base64` -> `raw_hcfg_section` -> `wasm_data_segment` -> `raw_const_array` (other native data section) -> `raw`.\n- **Any other encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data)`** (hex/base32/85/UTF-16/reversed/xor/zlib/multibyte+rolling xor/byte maps/\n  custom b64/split/int-array/strided/RC4/AES/TEA/ChaCha/stack-built); `hcfg_find` = first valid hit. Not the PK19 stub.\n- **xor key / config VALUE SHAPES** -- crc, key byte and campaign/domain/mutex/url re-roll per variant. Timed modes change the\n  SHAPE too: D23 campaign `BRNN-00V` -> `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-CATALOG-00V` -> `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol\n  `variant-000.c` -> `sample.c`; D24 also domain `node-00V.dayNN...` -> `<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid` (word: sync/hub/\n  core/mesh/relay/stage, D25-D26 also edge/cache/vault/proxy/node), mutex `Global\\HuntressBRNN_00V` -> `Global\\Huntress<12 uppercase\n  hex>`, url `.../api/BRNN-00V` -> `https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`; D27 shows ONE word pool for\n  domain, url host and url path (sync/hub/core/mesh/relay/stage/edge/cache/vault/proxy/node/gate), each drawn independently.\n  D28 false friend: campaign prefix `FF28-` (`FF28-000` single, `FF28-<8HEX>` timed) vs the family's `BR28-`; new keys\n  `host_model` (`workstation`) and `ipv4` (TEST-NET dotted quad) are asked too.\n  Rule: copy values verbatim from the decoded JSON/symtab; never regex-check a value shape or key on `00V` indices.\n- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ re-rolls per member in Mastery (d02, d04, d10 `pe`); labels from THIS member's header;\n  dispatch on MAGIC (`7f454c46`, `MZ`, `PK`, `\\0asm`, next `NEKO`). PE symbol fields = COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`. Extensions lie\n  about role, not container (D21 `.cmxs` = ELF ET_DYN). **ELF-worded backfill ids still apply to a PE re-roll** (D28 TT d10 `.exe`:\n  \"Read ELF e_shnum ... including index 0\" -> GM took FILE_HEADER.NumberOfSections, 9, no +1): map each ELF field to its PE twin.\n- **Member qualifier in the id (D15/D16/D21/D24)** -- peel the longest field prefix that is a `[^a-z0-9]+` token of exactly one\n  member name (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`, `loader`/`plugin`, `vulnerable`/`corrected` D24+D25, `gcc`/`tcc` D27,\n  `family_a`/`family_b`/`false_friend` D28 = basename `-`->`_`, MULTI-WORD; roles can be compiler names, so never hard-code the\n  vocabulary; `family` alone names TWO members -> take the longest token naming exactly one); the token can sit\n  BEFORE the field family (D24 `d24_analysis_corrected_format`, `..._corrected_config_url`). `sha256_K` = ARCHIVE order, never\n  sorted (D24: vulnerable is member 1).\n- **Member named in the QUESTION (D21)** -- after the qualifier peel, if >1 member remains, keep the one whose basename ends with\n  the token after `basename ends` / `Use the dNN--`. ORDER MATTERS (running it first dropped 26 ids on D21).\n- **Unqualified id over a twin pair / named subset (D24, D25, D27; D28)** -- \"Decode both dNN-- role members and require their\n  config objects to be byte-for-byte equal before using the common value\"; D28 \"Decode family-a.elf and family-b.elf ...\n  common FAMILY value; do not use false-friend.elf\": decode the members the question NAMES, drop the excluded one, assert equal\n  JSON, answer the common value. The excluded look-alike carries a DIFFERENT valid config (campaign `FF28-...` vs `BR28-...`), so\n  \"first member\" or \"all members agree\" logic is wrong here -- parse the include/exclude names from the question.\n- **Theme sidecar inside the member (D26)** -- jar entry `crash/trace.json` (`huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`, `kind`, `frames`\n  innermost-first), IDENTICAL in all 12 deliveries while config re-rolled. Rule: entry whose name ends `trace.json` (never a\n  fixed path), answer frames[0] verbatim; \"every frame in the primary classfile method-name set\" = set inclusion; missing =\n  `none`/`false`. Primary classfile (d07 and d26) = the manifest Main-Class, never a `$_main_closure1`; method_count = ALL\n  method_info rows incl. Groovy synthetics (10). Inner class names keep `Variant000` although basenames say `sample`.\n- **Member basename vocabulary (D22)** -- `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`; group by `dNN--` + extension/role tag only.\n- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22, D23)** -- primary assembly + `.runtimeconfig.json` (+ D22 `FSharp.Core.dll`); question:\n  \"primary managed assembly ... runtimeconfig and dependency DLL members are delivery support only\". Primary = the `.dll` whose\n  name is not a framework/dependency (FSharp.Core, System.*, Microsoft.*), i.e. the one carrying HCFG; hash ALL members.\n- **Stripped carry-over d01** -- re-rolls stripped in some sets (D15-D17 Mastery, D17/D19 TT, D23 Mastery set6): symbols/\n  disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, recover_code `none` (GM-confirmed; leaf-heuristic constants rejected). Pair by sha256.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` ids (2-12 sets; D27 11 x ~36 MB, D28 12 x ~17 MB), each its own delivery; each set's 1st question ends `Evidence\n  case: dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` (TT `dNN-tt-...`) = set->delivery map. Per-member caches key on\n  (delivery, member name) or sha256, never `id(bytes)` (D25: 5/9 sets cross-wired, see Pitfalls).\n- **kind / field sets per group** -- `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER (`64`/`62`) on d08/d15/d21 (dispatch on\n  `answer_format.kind`, which can change between fetches, D17); `has_<x>` = a structural marker of <x> in THIS member; old groups\n  gain ids over days (D8, D17, D28): answer by field name from THAT member's facts dict.\n- **Backfill #3 spec grammar (D28, 54 ids on d01-d27)** -- every new old-group id spells its rule: \"Evaluate this public predicate\n  ... true exactly when the final bytes [as Latin-1 or UTF-16LE] contain X [or any nonempty ELF symbol name contains Y]\"\n  (`has_nim/fpc/gnat_runtime`, `has_decoy_branch`); \"From ELF symbol-table entries with nonempty resolved names, count names that\n  match /re/\" (`d_symbol_count`, `crystal_symbol_count`, `handler_symbol_count`, `symbol_count`); \"sort ... join with one LF ...\n  SHA-256\" (`handler_symbols_sha256`, `method_names_sha256` over UNIQUE names); \"join digests with ':' ... SHA-256\"\n  (`structural_ordered_set_sha256`); byte scans (`conditional_branch_opcode_count`: 0x70-0x7f and 0f 80-8f in `.text`, one\n  left-to-right pass); header reads (`cli_runtime` = CLI header Major.Minor, `section_count`, PK19 `packing_key_1/2_hex`); new\n  config keys (`host_model`, `ipv4`); role-member config ids for the twin NOT asked before (`vulnerable_`, `symbolized_`,\n  `direct_`, `plugin_`, `gcc_`). Rule: implement the sentence literally (`lib.binary.generic_field` covers all of them); \"ELF\n  symbol-table entries\" = `.symtab` only (dupes kept), `.dynsym` ONLY when there is no `.symtab` (d13: 771 accepted, 1255 with\n  .dynsym rejected); a size id whose question names no magic = the day's own overlay magic (d20 `overlay_size` = len -\n  rfind(`RS20`) = 463; a generic `<2 caps><2 digits>` match gave 19, rejected).\n- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- CPU contention: re-measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py`; D25 TT\n  solve phase 8.0 s at 300 ids under load, D26 3.2 s (TT) / 3.9 s (10-set Mastery); isolated single ~0.6-1.2 s.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (K = archive order within the group) |\n| `readelf -h -S` hint, ELF header questions | `readelf -hSW`, `readelf -sW`; `readelf -p .huntress` for the custom-section `marker` (D1, re-asked D17) |\n| \"constant returned by recover_code\" / `disassembly` | `objdump -d -M intel --no-show-raw-insn` around `<recover_code>`; capstone on the FUNC symbol's st_value..st_size bytes |\n| Stripped C build, no `.symtab` | answer the absence the question defines (`[]`/`none`); only as recon find the leaf `b8 imm32 c3` (`lib.binary.recover_return_constants`) |\n| C++ / \"mangled\" / \"vtable\" / \"RTTI\" | `nm -C` / `c++filt`; `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`; `score` method `_ZNK<len><Class>5scoreEPKc`; PE: `objdump -t file.exe` (COMDAT names) |\n| `PE32+` MinGW `.exe` | `objdump -t` (COFF symbols + string table), `pefile` (Machine, OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic, sections incl. `.hcfg`) |\n| \"CLI metadata\", `.dll` + `runtimeconfig.json`, `BSJB` | `ilspycmd file.dll` or Python `dnfile`; config = `<PrivateImplementationDetails>` FieldRVA static array; `BSJB v4.0.30319` |\n| F# (AssemblyRef `FSharp.Core`, `FSharpSignatureData.*` resources, `$Program`, closures `name@<line>`) + big `FSharp.Core.dll` member / VB.NET (AssemblyRef `Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core`, `StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_<n>`, `Operators::CompareString`) | Same as C#: `pe_cli` / `i386` (AnyCPU ILONLY 0x14c) / `v4.0.30319`; answer from the PRIMARY dll only; raw `grep -abo HCFG` -> first crc-valid hit (D22 `.text` + overlay copy; D23 PE overlay only) |\n| P/Invoke / \"bridge\" / \"crossing\" 