theme \"call graph / no injection\" unasked, CORRECT T+11 s). **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"\n(static-unpacking)** = ONE GnuCOBOL ELF (11 KB, `libcob.so.1`, stripped) whose HCFG is NOT in the image: a `PK19` overlay is\nappended after the section-header table (`PK19|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le len|sha256[32]|packed`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`, sha256-check,\nHCFG at out[0]). FIRST day whose prompt theme WAS asked on its own group: config_* only after unpacking + NEW `overlay_offset`\n(offset of the last magic) / `overlay_size` (file length - offset). The question text spelled the whole stub; 228 ids = 216 + 12,\nno backfill; CORRECT T+2:25, TT 4 s / Mastery (5 sets) 10 s first try; overlay 10808/424 constant across variants.\n**D20 \"Resourceful\" (resources-and-overlays)** = ONE Haskell ELF (GHC 9.12.2, 1.2 MB, dynamic libgmp, not stripped) + a 463-B\n`RS20` overlay at e_shoff+e_shnum*64: `RS20|ver@4|u32le res_len@8|u16le scratch_len@12|sha256(scratch)@16|HCFG resource@48 (RAW)|\nscratch` (\"private-scratch:<campaign>:inert-only\"). 240 ids = 228 + 12; NEW `hcfg_resource_size` (= u32le @8, 380). The prebuilt\nRS20/question-spec unpacker + raw HCFG scan banked 239 ids at T+27 s; one field branch -> CORRECT T+49 s, 0 wrong; TT 4.8 s /\nMastery 9.3 s first try; overlay constant across variants. D19-D20 = a \"hidden storage\" arc (packed overlay -> resource overlay;\nprompt: \"resources, overlays, bytes past the end of the sections ... map every boundary\").\n**D21 \"Shared Custody\" (shared-library-boundaries)** = a LOADER + PLUGIN pair: `-loader.elf` (780 KB OCaml 4.02.3 native PIE,\ndebug_info, NEEDED libm/libdl/libc, Dynlink `caml_natdynlink_open`/`caml_dlopen`; NO HCFG) + `-plugin.cmxs` (9 KB ET_DYN OCaml\nnatdynlink plugin, exports `caml_plugin_header`/`caml_globals`/`camlPlugin_000*`, `Caml2007D002` dynheader, HCFG RAW in `.data`).\n252 ids = 240 + 12: `loader_machine`/`plugin_machine` (integer 62) + config_* twice (unqualified ids name the plugin IN THE\nQUESTION, plus `plugin_config_*`). The theme (exports/imports/handshake) was NOT asked. Only a routing change (question-named\nmember, applied after the qualifier peel) -> CORRECT T+1:33, 0 wrong; TT 4.2 s / Mastery 9.9 s first try.\n**D22 \"Bridge Troll\" (managed-native-bridge)** = an F# .NET 8 group of 3: `d22--sample.dll` (18.8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY, BSJB\n`v4.0.30319`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (same bytes as d03's) + `FSharp.Core.dll` (5.7 MB stock dependency, constant sha256\nacross sets). Bridge = 2 P/Invoke ImplMap rows (`getpid`@ModuleRef `libc`, `GetCurrentProcessId`@`kernel32.dll`, Winapi), trace\n`fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace`. HCFG RAW in `.text` (F# array blob) + an identical copy as a PE overlay; question: \"first\nrecord that validates\". 264 ids = 252 + 12 (3 sha256 + the d03 field family verbatim); theme NOT asked. All members silently\nrenamed `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`. Carried-over solver -> CORRECT T+47 s, 0 wrong; TT 12.3 s / Mastery (6 sets,\n1584 ids) 18.2 s first try. FIRST day re-using an old RUNTIME with a new language (.NET: C# D3 -> F# D22).\n**D23 \"Trust Issues\" (anti-analysis-recognition)** = a VB.NET .NET 8 group of 2: `d23--sample.dll` (8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY,\n.text/.rsrc/.reloc, BSJB `v4.0.30319`, AssemblyRefs System.Runtime/Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/System.Text.Json/System.Console,\n`StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_0`8`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (d03's bytes). Predicates (theme, UNASKED):\n`Debugger.get_IsAttached`, `Stopwatch.StartNew`/`get_ElapsedTicks` (clock), `Environment.get_ProcessorCount`,\n`GetEnvironmentVariable(\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\")` vs workstation/analysis/sandbox -> branch success/decoy/failure, trace\n`vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/`inert_predicate_only`, field `analysis_detected`. No ImplMap, no FieldRVA. HCFG RAW ONCE as\na PE overlay right after `.reloc` (7680 = EOF-380). 276 ids = 264 + 12 (2 sha256 + d22 family + `xor_key_hex`). Carried-over\nsolver -> CORRECT T+84 s (22 s download), 0 wrong; TT 13.0 s / Mastery 7 sets (1932 ids) 7.9 s first try. NEW in timed modes:\nvalue SHAPES re-rolled (`BR23-<8 uppercase hex>` campaign, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol `sample.c`) -- harmless\nfor a verbatim-copying solver. THIRD .NET language (C# D3, F# D22, VB.NET D23) and the first BEHAVIOUR (evasion) theme.\n**D24 \"Spot the Difference\" (patch-diffing)** = a Scala 2.13 TWIN pair: `d24--sample-vulnerable.jar` (member 1) +\n`d24--sample-corrected.jar` (member 2), ~4 KB each, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Scala factory`, classes\n`Day24<Role>000.class` (static forwarder, Main-Class) + `Day24<Role>000$.class` (module: `MODULE$`, base64 HCFG `ldc` in\n`<clinit>`, `decodeConfig`, `score(String)I`, `main`), `ScalaSignature`/`ScalaSig`, scala-library not bundled. Prompt: \"Two\nbuilds, one fix. Diff the vulnerable function against its corrected twin and pinpoint exactly what changed -- then prove the old\none was really broken.\" The fix (UNASKED): only `score` changed -- vulnerable `if (s.nonEmpty) s.charAt(0) else -1` NPEs on\n`null` (CWE-476); corrected `Option(s).filter(_.nonEmpty).map(_.charAt(0)).getOrElse(-1)` (+3 invokedynamic lambdas). `main`\nidentical (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL lookupswitch -> decoy/success/failure), trace `scala_patch_diff_trace`/`benign_control_and_\nreversion_only` + `control_positive`. 288 ids = 276 + 12: 2 sha256, `vulnerable_format`/`corrected_format` (`jar`), 4\nUNQUALIFIED config_* (\"decode both role members, require byte-for-byte equal config, use the common value\"), 4\n`corrected_config_*`. Carried-over solver, ZERO new code -> CORRECT T+35 s, 0 wrong; TT 5.0 s / Mastery 8 sets (2304 ids) 8.4 s\nfirst try. The whole contract was reworded into specs (sha256 \"ZIP central-directory order (1-based)\", HCFG layout + JAR carrier\nrule \"Base64-alphabet UTF-8 constants >= 80 chars\"); timed modes re-shaped domain/mutex/url too (`<word>-<8hex>.dayNN...`,\n`Global\\Huntress<12HEX>`, `/<word>/<10hex>`).\n*