_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol,\nhas_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset,\nhcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size,\nhcfg_resource_size, `<role>_machine` (D21 loader/plugin, integer), `<role>_format` + `<role>_config_*` (D24 vulnerable/corrected; D27 `<role>_machine` + `<role>_format` + `gcc_config_*`, roles gcc/tcc), `crash_fault_method`, `crash_frames_match_methods` (D26); D28 roles `false_friend`/`family_a`/`family_b` + backfill #3: `structural_artifact_count`, `structural_ordered_set_sha256`, `config_host_model`, `config_ipv4`, `vtable_symbol`, `cli_runtime`, `has_decoy_branch`, `has_<nim|fpc|gnat>_runtime`, `symbol_count`, `d_symbol_count`, `crystal_symbol_count`, `handler_symbol_count`, `handler_symbols_sha256`, `class_count`, `class_name`, `section_count`, `conditional_branch_opcode_count`, `packing_key_1_hex`/`packing_key_2_hex`, `method_names_sha256`, `plugin_hcfg_offset`, `plugin_config_crc32_hex`.\nRemaining risks: (0000000) the D28 cluster theme ASKED or extended: `family_members` (JSON list of member names), `false_friend`/\n`stranger` member name, `family_size`, per-pair similarity (byte-diff count, `.text` sha256 equal?, shared-function count, ssdeep/\nTLSH score), cluster label per member, \"which config is the family's\" with 4-6 look-alikes and several strangers, possibly\nstripped and with the false friend's config byte-identical except one key -- answer from bytes per the question's stated metric;\n(000000) the D27 attribution theme ASKED (`<role>_compiler`/`toolchain`/`compiler_version`/`linker`/`libc`/\n`debug_format`/`producer`/`opt_level` per build, or \"which member was built by X\") -- label spelling unknown (expect an enum like\nD17; lowercase tool names gcc/tcc/clang), facts must come from producer/sections/symbols because `.comment` was stripped; (00000) a NATIVE crash artifact (core/minidump/sanitizer log) next to an ELF/PE: signal/exception code, faulting\nRIP -> function + instruction, frame list by unwinding, fault-address class -- or the D26 sidecar idea in another container\n(ELF section/PE resource/separate member) with frames as `Class.method(File:line)` or addresses; (0000) the twin arc's facts asked as fields on d24/d25 (changed function, bug class/CWE, trigger input, gating\nenv vars + values, exception class, guard constant) or a NATIVE twin whose diff needs function matching; (000) the D24 diff asked as fields (changed method name/descriptor, bug class / CWE, trigger input, outcome\nper build) or a NATIVE twin pair whose diff must be found by function matching (stripped?) -- see the patch-diff gaps; (00) the D23 predicates asked as fields (predicate list, env var name, compared host-model values, branch per\nhost model, timing threshold, `analysis_detected` verdict) or an obfuscation sequel (encrypted strings/IL, anti-disassembly,\nflattened control flow) where the HCFG is only reachable through a decoder; (0) the bridge theme backfilled on d22 (ImplMap module/import names, callconv, marshaled types, call sites) or\nan FFI bridge on another runtime (JNI, ctypes, N-API) with a native member; (1) the structure arc continues (linking internals:\nrelocations/GOT/PLT, symbol versions, RPATH/RUNPATH, TLS/IFUNC, or a PE DLL loader/plugin pair) with 2+ role members -- route by question text; (2) a backfill of the D18-D21 themes\n(call graph, PK19/RS20 header fields, NEEDED/exports/dlopen target/plugin header); (3) Neko bytecode labels (VM machine/arch);\n(4) D26 JVM classfile member; (5) per-language fact backfills (D8-D21 groups); (6) a 3+-member group (loader + several plugins,\ndecoy HCFG in the loader).\n\nTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\nInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-